Q: Run code in a MonoBehaviour whenever another component is added A: <p>Sadly, there is no built-in <code>OnComponentAdded</code> method in Unity's MonoBehaviour API.</p>
<p>However, you can achieve similar behavior by using the <code>MonoBehaviour.onEnable()</code> hook to detect when another component is enabled on your GameObject. For example :</p>
<pre><code>using System.Collections;  
using System.Collections.Generic;  
using UnityEngine; 

public class MyMonoBehaviour : MonoBehaviour
{
    private void OnEnable()
    {
        Component[] components = GetComponents&lt;ITestComponent&gt;();
        foreach (var component in components)
        {
            Debug.Log(&quot;Component added!&quot;);
        }
    }

    public interface ITestComponent { }
}
</code></pre>
<p>This approach has its limitations, as it only works when a component is enabled. You may want to explore other options:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Use an <code>OnTriggerEnter</code> or similar callback for physics events</p>
</li>
<li><p>Create a custom listener system using Unity's Events API (available in 2018 and later versions).</p>
</li>
<li><p>Use the <code>MonoBehaviour.onAwake()</code> method, which runs before any other methods, including those triggered by other components</p>
</li>
</ul>

Q: Pointers in A Decomposition Function A: <p>It should be</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>long foo;
double bar;
decompose(3.14, &amp;foo, &amp;bar);
// use `foo` and `bar` now
printf(&quot;original: %.2f ==&gt; decomposed into %ld and %f\n&quot;, 3.14, foo, bar);
</code></pre>

Q: Using std::apply in a class template A: <p>In addition to the answer already given, your code can be simplified to this:</p>
<pre><code>template&lt;class... Types&gt;
class ViewPath : public Path {
public:
    ViewPath(Types... args)
       : function{[args...] {
           (std::println(&quot;{}&quot;, args), ...); // or whatever you want
       }}
    {}
    void executeFunction() const override {
        function();
    }
private:
    std::function&lt;void()&gt; function;
};
</code></pre>

Q: It is necessary in PHP code where there is a js code to output, for example, through an alert variable A: <p>You can't use <code>&lt;?php</code> tags inside each other. It makes no sense anyway - you're already in the PHP block, you don't need to open it again. And for similar reasons you can't use <code>echo</code> inside another <code>echo</code> command. And again it makes no sense anyway, you're already echoing, so why repeat the same instruction before you've finished the first one?</p>
<p>To generate the text you want, just use <a href="https://www.php.net/manual/en/language.operators.string.php" rel="nofollow noreferrer">string concatenation</a> with the <code>.</code> (dot) operator:</p>
<pre><code>echo '&lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;
  alert(&quot;'.$locationName.'&quot;); 
  var img = &quot;'.$locationName.'&quot;; 
  document.getElementById(&quot;image_location&quot;).src = img;
  &lt;/script&gt;';
</code></pre>

Q: Trying to create a looping cards in PHP (bootstrap) A: <p>I think you left part of your card out of your loop. I'm guessing you've got one <code>&lt;div class="card"&gt;</code> containing many <code>&lt;div class="card-body"&gt;</code>s.</p>

<p>I would leave the <code>&lt;div class="row"&gt;</code> out of your loop, but everything inside that should be part of the loop.</p>

<pre><code>&lt;div class="row"&gt;
    &lt;?php

                        $query = mysqli_query($koneksi, "SELECT * FROM article ORDER BY datae DESC");

                        // looping Artikel
                        while($artikel = mysqli_fetch_array($query)){
                            echo "&lt;div class='col-12 col-md-4'&gt;";
                            echo "&lt;div class='card mb-4 shadow-sm'&gt;";
                            echo "&lt;div class='card-body'&gt;";
                            echo "&lt;a class='card-title' href='artikel.php?id=".$artikel['id']."' /&gt;".$title['title']."&lt;/a&gt;";
                            echo "&lt;p class='article-date'&gt;Oleh &lt;b&gt;".$author['author']."&lt;/b&gt;, pada ".$article['date']."&lt;/p&gt;";
                            echo "&lt;/div&gt;";
                            echo "&lt;/div&gt;";
                            echo "&lt;/div&gt;";
                        }

                    ?&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
